# Expected vs observed outcomes per state — `gap.Gap` fixture

States are the Haxe syntax shapes in `fixture/gap/Gap.hx`. "Observed" is what the
verified generation actually emitted (`generated/gap/Gap.swift`, byte-identical
reproduction in `generated-repro/gap/Gap.swift`). "Expected (when correct)" is
the Swift the fixed backend must emit so that `swiftc -typecheck` passes: every
`TiqianArray<Int32>` that crosses into a `ReadOnlyArray<Int32>`-typed position
must be wrapped as `ReadOnlyArray(...)`.

`ReadOnlyArray<Element>` and `TiqianArray<Element>` are two unrelated `final`
classes (per `REPORT.md` §2: `SwiftRuntime.hx:384` and `SwiftRuntime.hx:486`;
`ReadOnlyArray` wraps a `TiqianArray` in a `backing` field). There is no implicit
conversion, so every unwrapped crossing is a hard `swiftc` type error.

Line numbers below refer to `gap/Gap.swift` as generated.

## Defective states (7 shapes, 12 `swiftc` errors)

### S1 `Gap.switchLocal` — switch expression as initializer, dest `ReadOnlyArray<Int>`
Haxe: `var view:ReadOnlyArray<Int> = switch (choice) { case One: sourceFirst(); case Two: sourceSecond(); };`
Backend path: `stmtLines:690` → `switchBindingLines` → `switchExpression` (`SwiftExpr.hx:5523`), call site 691.
Observed (Gap.swift:39-46):
```swift
let view = ({ () -> ReadOnlyArray<Int32> in
switch choice {
    case .one:
        return Gap.sourceFirst()
    case .two:
        return Gap.sourceSecond()
}
})()
```
Expected (when correct): the closure arms must be boundary-converted:
```swift
        return ReadOnlyArray(Gap.sourceFirst())
        ...
        return ReadOnlyArray(Gap.sourceSecond())
```
Observed defect — quoted from `evidence/swiftc-gap-final.log` (line 42):
```
.../gen-gap/gap/Gap.swift:42:24: error: cannot convert value of type 'TiqianArray<Int32>' to closure result type 'ReadOnlyArray<Int32>'
```

