## Control states (convert correctly; typecheck passes)

### C1 `Gap.controlTernary` — ternary initializer (funnel IS reached, call site 746)
Observed (Gap.swift:34): `let view = flag ? ReadOnlyArray(Gap.sourceFirst()) : ReadOnlyArray(Gap.sourceSecond())`
Correct. This is the contrast proving the conversion exists — it is just not applied on the S1-S7 paths.

### C2 `GapExtra.ifReturnPosition` — ternary in return position
Observed (Gap.swift:86): `return flag ? ReadOnlyArray(Gap.sourceFirst()) : ReadOnlyArray(Gap.sourceSecond())`
Correct.

### C3 `GapStatics.values` — static read-only field (separate producer, `SwiftDecl.hx:599/604`)
Observed (Gap.swift:106): `public static let values: ReadOnlyArray<Int32> = ReadOnlyArray(TiqianArray<Int32>([41]))`
Correct — and note it bypasses `lowerArrayBoundary` entirely (`REPORT.md` §5).

### C4 `GapPaths2.switchStatementPath` — statement-position switch
Observed (Gap.swift:153-155): `view = ReadOnlyArray(Gap.sourceFirst())` / `view = ReadOnlyArray(Gap.sourceSecond())`
Correct: statement arms render through `binop` → `assignmentValue`, which converts.

### C5 `GapPaths2.tryStatementAssignPath` — statement-position try
Observed (Gap.swift:166-168): `view = ReadOnlyArray(Gap.sourceFirst())` / `view = ReadOnlyArray(Gap.sourceSecond())`
